1. Why do you want to work in the United States?
Sample Answer: "I am excited about the opportunity to work in the United States because it is a hub of innovation and technological advancement. The kind of exposure and experience I would get working with leading companies and experts in my field is incomparable. It is not just about better job opportunities, but also about personal growth and the chance to broaden my horizon."
2. Which company are you going to work for?
Sample Answer: "I will be working for XYZ Corporation, a leading name in the IT sector. With a global presence and commitment to innovation, XYZ has made significant strides in big data and artificial intelligence, areas that align with my interests and expertise."

3. What is your job profile?
Sample Answer: "As a data analyst, I will be responsible for interpreting complex datasets and converting them into actionable insights. My role involves understanding business problems, cleaning and pre-processing data, building predictive models, and presenting findings in a clear and compelling manner. I will be collaborating with different teams to help improve business operations and decision-making processes."
4. What is your highest educational qualification?
Sample Answer: "I hold a Master's degree in Computer Science from XYZ University."

5. How did you find your job?
Sample Answer: "I found the job through a job portal and then proceeded to apply directly on the company's website."
6. What will be your salary in the US?
Sample Answer: "I have been offered an annual salary package of $85,000 by XYZ Corporation. In addition to the basic pay, my compensation package also includes health benefits and performance bonuses. This will not only cover my living expenses in the US but will also allow me to save for the future."
Now, have you ever wondered why these questions matter? What are the interviewers looking for? Well, as a US visa interviewer, one of their primary objectives is to verify the authenticity and validity of your intentions and credentials. They also want to ensure that you have the ability and the means to sustain your life in the United States.

7. How long do you plan on staying in the US?
Sample Answer: "My H1-B visa allows me to work in the US for three years, extendable to six years. After this period, I plan to return to my home country. I view this stint as a great opportunity to learn and grow as a professional, and then apply those learnings back home."

8. Can you describe your project?
Sample Answer: "Absolutely, I'd be happy to describe my project. I will be working on a project that involves the development of a predictive analytics tool for the retail industry. This tool is designed to predict consumer buying behavior based on historical data and trend analysis.
The main aim is to help retailers understand what their customers are likely to buy, when, and why. This, in turn, assists them in making informed decisions about inventory management, sales promotions, and product placements.
My role in the project will be as a Data Analyst. I will be primarily responsible for data mining, preprocessing the data, and developing algorithms that can accurately predict customer behavior. In addition, I will also be involved in visualizing the data in a comprehensible manner so that the insights generated can be easily understood by the decision-makers."

What is your current address?
Sample Answer: "My current address is XYZ”

10. Have you ever been to the US before?
Sample Answer: "No, I haven't been to the US before."

11. Why are you changing from F1 (Student) visa to H1-B visa?

Sample Answer: "Upon completing my studies, I was offered a position with XYZ Corporation. To legally work with them, I need to change my visa status from F1 to H1-B."
12. When does your H1-B start?
Sample Answer: "My H1-B visa is set to start on October 1st, 2023. I plan to travel a couple of weeks before to settle in and get accustomed to the new environment."

13. Will you come back to your home country?
Sample Answer: "Yes, after my H1-B visa term ends, I plan to return to my home country."

14. How will this job in the US benefit you when you return home?
Sample Answer: "The global exposure and advanced skill set I will acquire in the US will significantly enhance my job prospects when I return home."

15. Do you have any relatives in the US?
Sample Answer: "Yes, I have a brother who lives in the US. However, my long-term plans remain rooted in my home country. I view the H1-B visa as a temporary arrangement that will allow me to gain invaluable experience in my field and further my career."

16. Who is sponsoring your H1-B visa?
Sample Answer: "My H1-B visa is being sponsored by XYZ Corporation. They are covering all the expenses related to the visa application and processing. This sponsorship is part of my employment agreement with them."

17. How many people work in your current office?
Sample Answer: "We have around 50 employees at our current office."

18. How long have you been working for your current employer?
Sample Answer: "I have been working with my current employer for two years."

19. How will you manage your expenses in the US?
Sample Answer: "The salary offered by XYZ Corporation is competitive and more than sufficient to cover my living expenses in the US. I've also done my research on the cost of living in the city I'll be moving to and have prepared a monthly budget to manage my expenses effectively."

20. Can I see your H1-B Visa Stamping and other documents?
Sample Answer: "Certainly, I have all my documents organized and ready for your review. Here are my passport, H1-B Visa Stamping, I-797 form, and employment offer letter from XYZ Corporation."





I have got my H1B approved.

Location: Hyderabad

Time: Jan 9th, 9:00 AM, be there before 45 mins.

Entered the line at 8:40, and took 90 minutes to go to the counter.

Officer: Good morning, how are you doing.

Me: Morning officer, I'm doing good.

Asked passport and handed it over.

Officer: For which Visa you are here for?

Me: H1B

Officer: Please hand over LCA

Handed over LCA

VO went through the papers

Officer: Your sponsoring company?

Me: Said my current company

Officer: Which state are you traveling to?

Me: NY

Officer: Do you have an end client?

Me: Yes, said client name

Officer: How much salary you will receive?

Me: Mentioned the amount from LCA.

Officer: What will be your role?

Me: Told the role that I will be working in US. As per LCA.

Officer: What will you do for this client?

Me: I'll be working on their internal sales processing application, managing and maintaining the data as per protocols. Integrating with other systems. Providing a simplified UI for the business associates so that they can do their work and if they make any changes we have to pass the information back to the applications from which we got the data through the same integration points.



I have said the entire thing, while I am doing so, VO started typing on her computer and when I stopped she gave me the blue card saying 'Your Visa has been approved and you will receive it in a few days. Please go through the rules and regulation from this card.'

I said thanks and left the counter.



